Orin Stage uses the Ubuntu distribution Python, but bundles an exact private
Python application closure under /usr/lib/orin-stage/venv.  This preserves one
application dependency contract across Jammy and Noble while keeping CPython,
the compiler toolchain, and system libraries distro-provided.

All Python sdists and the Cargo vendor tree are verified source inputs in the
separate deps orig component.  The package build is intentionally offline once
Build-Depends have been installed from Ubuntu.

This is a PPA-oriented MVP packaging model, not a claim of Debian archive
upstream-policy suitability.
